  <prompt>
    Carry the `AnchoredAnnotation` Path-A deviation into explicit code-review sign-off. Per CLAUDE.md §6.5
    Path A, a project-scoped exception must be documented + rationalized + reviewer-approved at the point of
    decision. The charter §3.4 rule bans local MemoryItem variants; the R2 design argues `AnchoredAnnotation`
    is NOT a MemoryItem variant (document-adjacent positional UI state, never written via `memory.*`, never
    retrieved by the Context Binder, never in the memory review/delete view; tenant+matter scoped). This task
    verifies task 060's implementation matches that argument and obtains reviewer sign-off — or, if the argument
    is rejected, escalates to negotiate a MemoryItem sub-type WITH the core (never a silent local variant).
  </prompt>

